From: richie-rich90454 <rjiang880@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0011/0014] Disable Microsoft settings sync

This patch drops the settings-sync workbench contribution (views,
commands, status entries) from the shared workbench entry. The sync
store was already unreachable without a product
configurationSyncStore key, and the Microsoft account providers are
gone with patch 0009, so no sync path can reach Microsoft. Sync, if
ever wanted, points at platform storage, not Microsoft.

Touches:
  - workbench entry (userDataSync contribution import)

Verification: no sync endpoints in the no-network test.

---
diff --git a/src/vs/workbench/workbench.common.main.ts b/src/vs/workbench/workbench.common.main.ts
index 285fea2..6e4b422 100644
--- a/src/vs/workbench/workbench.common.main.ts
+++ b/src/vs/workbench/workbench.common.main.ts
@@ -351,7 +351,6 @@ import './contrib/languageStatus/browser/languageStatus.contribution.js';
 import './contrib/authentication/browser/authentication.contribution.js';
 
 // User Data Sync
-import './contrib/userDataSync/browser/userDataSync.contribution.js';
 
 // User Data Profiles
 import './contrib/userDataProfile/browser/userDataProfile.contribution.js';
